-- title:
--   Branch prime (t,y) at a crossing-model node
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a Noetherian local domain and let $W$ be a discrete valuation ring that is a domain and is complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal; let $\pi \in W$ be irreducible and let $E$ be a natural number with $1 \le E$. Write $M =$ `UVCrossingModel W (π ^ E)` for the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,W$, i.e. $W[[X_0,X_1]]$, by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - \pi^E$, and let `const (π ^ E) w` denote the class of the constant series with value $w$; the model carries distinguished elements `U (π ^ E)` and `V (π ^ E)`, whose product is `const (π ^ E) (π ^ E)`. Assume given a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the $\mathfrak m_B$-adic completion `AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal B) B` onto $M$, and elements $t, x, y \in B$ such that $\iota$ carries the canonical image of $t$ to `const (π ^ E) π`, the image of $x$ to $\gamma_U \cdot$ `U (π ^ E)` and the image of $y$ to $\gamma_V \cdot$ `V (π ^ E)` for some units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of $M$. Then: there is a unit $u$ of $B$ with $xy = t^E u$; the ideal $(t,y)$ of $B$ is prime and does not contain $x$; every prime ideal $\mathfrak q$ of $B$ with $t \in \mathfrak q$, $x \notin \mathfrak q$ and $\mathfrak q \ne \mathfrak m_B$ equals $(t,y)$; and $(t,y)$ has height $1$.
--
--   This is the algebraic description of one branch through a split ordinary double point of thickness $E$ on a normal model of a curve over a discrete valuation ring: the component along which $x$ does not vanish identically is the height-one prime $(t,y)$, characterised as the unique non-maximal prime containing $t$ but not $x$. It is used to locate the centre of a valuation on such a model, in [`AlgebraicCurve.NodeAnnulusEngine.isIntegral_and_evalAt_mem_of_mem_ends_of_forall_mem_toValuationSubring`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.NodeAnnulusEngine.isIntegral_and_evalAt_mem_of_mem_ends_of_forall_mem_toValuationSubring) and in the Igusa-trichotomy results for the auxiliary levels of modular curves.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_exists_mul_eq_pow_mul_and_isPrime_span_pair_and_height_eq_one_of_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_uvCrossingModel.lean

